Actually, this is on the original subject; I waited until the thread was
finished to reply, since I'm catching up on (what didn't expire from) three
weeks' worth of news.

Phones and phone books:  model them after the real thing.

Phones come in two forms:  objects and traps.  The former are "cellular"
phones --- they co$t to use, and co$t more if you use them on a different
level than they were found on --- roaming, you know.  ;-)

The latter are phone booths.  I don't think polymorph into Superman would be
workable (or legal...) but a wand of polymorph applied in a phone booth
might make you into a demon-like creature of the appropriate gender and
alignment.  This effect, of course, would not be permanent.  Phone booths
cost less to use than cellphones, but you may have to wait in line behind a
monster.  (And you may find that the phone has been wrecked by orcs!)

Phone books are modified spellbooks.  They only list things on the level they
are found on.  If it is decided to support "pre-creating" objects on
un-visited levels, one might add a special shop with phone books for various
levels; if not, the system described here doesn't require pre-knowledge of
levels.  The types of books would vary, also:  white pages (anything you call
is a monster or etc.; not too useful), yellow pages (shops), and specialized
phone books which would cover subsets of the two (e.g. orc white pages,
delicatessen yellow pages).

(Of course, I have to wonder if ther'll be a radio object with phone patch --
no businesses, please, or the Kops come after you!  [ ;-) ]  (See .sig.))

